WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.670 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  this was daniel ortega's fourth  consecutive swearing-in ceremony flanked  by his wife rosalio murillo his vice  president he vowed to improve conditions  in nicaragua the second poorest country  in the americas after haiti retro  we are here again with a clean slate to  build peace to assure that nicaraguans  have a dignified life to eradicate  poverty in this country with sovereignty  and freedom  the president of cuba and venezuela were  there and also delegations from iran  bolivia russia and china  but ortega was snubbed by almost  everyone else  november's presidential elections have  been dismissed as illegitimate by much  of the international community the  majority of ortega's competitors were  imprisoned so they could not run and  thousands of others have gone into exile  and legitimacy is not an issue  for ortega he managed to essentially  consummate  uh his uh  his uh his plan uh to establish  a full  and classic uh latin american  dictatorship in nicaragua  hours before the ceremony the european  union and the united states announced  new sanctions against high-ranking  military and communications officials as  well as members of the ortega family  but exiled opponent monica baltodano a  former sandinista commander who once  fought alongside ortega questions their  effectiveness  they demonstrate that the international  community realizes what's happening in  nicaragua and that's why it imposes  sanctions they have a moral effect a  kind of consolation but in practical  terms they'll have little impact  while ortega celebrated his latest  inauguration  some 170 political prisoners languished  in what human rights advocates describe  as cruel and inhumane conditions  one of them is  my husband is losing his memory and he's  in a deep depression after spending more  than 100 days in a punishment isolation  cell  he can't remember the names or faces of  our daughters  ortega made no mention of his  pre-election promised to initiate a  dialogue with his political opponents  that may explain why most nicaraguans  whom al jazeera consulted about the  inauguration  preferred to say nothing at all lucia  newman al jazeera

